            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/jowc.2016.25.Sup3.S10</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following a coronary bypass surgery, a vein donor site became infected and failed to heal despite use of antibiotics and a variety of topical treatments. Octenilin Wound Gel not only helped to promote healing, but also increased the patient's ability to tolerate dressing changes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
